reels.useGuidance:
Intended coverage (planned, not verified output): this silent 8-second identity-first neutral turntable is meant to provide:
- a frontal full-body hold;
- one steady camera orbit of a stationary Riley showing both three-quarter views, both profiles and the full back;
- a return frontal hold;
- a held frontal face close-up.

Intended uses:
- facial likeness with the round thin silver glasses;
- natural body proportions;
- side and rear silhouettes;
- the volume and shape of the auburn-brown hair worn in a low ponytail with face-framing wisps;
- continuity of the one outfit: white scoop-neck tank top, heather-grey drawstring shorts and bare feet.

Limits:
- The supplied photos show only frontal views, so the side and rear hair, ponytail and clothing are conservative continuations rather than observed detail.
- The hair is planned as the pulled-back ponytail seen in the photos, not loose or tucked-behind-the-ear hair.
- There is no articulation, expression range, hand detail or speech.

Before reuse, inspect the views actually generated. Check that:
- the face, glasses and ponytail match across all views;
- the proportions were not slimmed or altered;
- the tank top, shorts and drawstring stay consistent, with no added logos, hair accessories or other accessories;
- the person stayed stationary while the camera moved;
- the back and profile views are clean.

Discard or regenerate any segment that drifts.

